---
const zx = @import("zx");
const QuickExample = @import("../../overview/overview.zx").QuickExample;
const Greeting = @import("./greeting.mdzx").render;

pub const meta = .{
    .title = "MDZX",
    .description = "Markdown + ZX components, full scenario tour",
};

pub const options: zx.PageOptions = .{};

/// Request context for expressions in the markdown body.
var ctx: zx.PageContext = undefined;

pub fn Page(c: zx.PageContext) zx.Component {
    ctx = c;
    return zx.mdzx.page(@This(), c);
}
---

# MDZX

Markdown pages with embedded ZX, and an explicit `PageContext` when you need it.

You are on:

{ctx.request.pathname}

Also see the pure markdown sibling: [Pure Markdown](/examples/md).

<QuickExample />

## Component with props

MDZX components declare `Props` (and usually `var props`); `render` is generated for you.

<Greeting name="Ziex" />

## Formatting

Use **bold**, *italic*, ***bold italic***, ~~strike~~, and `inline code`.

Escaped: \*not emphasis\*

[Home](/) · [Examples](/examples) · <https://ziex.dev>

![Ziex logo alt](/favicon.ico)

